{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cet94cPrV8t7eLGZRnKeG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my analysis of the repository, here are my findings:\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- Shipment entity and status enum: `/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/Shipment.kt` (lines 9-27)\n- ShipmentController with create/get/list endpoints: `/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentController.kt` (lines 26-44)\n- InMemoryShipmentRepository: `/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentRepository.kt`\n- ApiException hierarchy: `/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiExceptions.kt` (ConflictException on line 22-24, ResourceNotFoundException on line 18-20)\n- ErrorCode enum: `/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiError.kt` (lines 31-37)\n- GlobalExceptionHandler: `/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/GlobalExceptionHandler.kt`\n\n**Conventions this repository follows:**\n1. State transitions are returned as the full updated entity (see ShipmentController.create, OrderController patterns)\n2. 404 errors use `ResourceNotFoundException` with `ErrorCode.SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND` (ShipmentController:49-52)\n3. 409 errors use `ConflictException` (ShipmentController:29-32)\n4. All endpoints return the same error envelope via GlobalExceptionHandler (ApiError with code, message, fields)\n5. Tests use MockMvc with jsonPath assertions for both success and error cases\n6. Tests check both status codes and error envelope shape\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `ShipmentController.kt` - Add the confirm endpoint\n2. `ApiError.kt` - Add a new ErrorCode for invalid shipment state (409 on CANCELLED)\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` - Add tests for the confirm endpoint\n\n**Risks:**\n1. Breaking existing tests if the endpoint doesn't follow the same patterns\n2. Not handling the idempotent case correctly (already CONFIRMED should succeed)\n3. Using the wrong HTTP status code for state conflicts\n\n**Open questions:**\nNone - the ticket is explicit about all four cases and their status codes.\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed changes:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt**: Add a new ErrorCode enum value `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS` to handle the 409 conflict when confirming a CANCELLED shipment.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt**: Add a new endpoint `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` that:\n   - Retrieves the shipment by ID\n   - Throws `ResourceNotFoundException` if not found (404)\n   - Throws `ConflictException` if status is CANCELLED (409)\n   - Updates status to CONFIRMED if currently CREATED\n   - Returns the updated shipment with 200 status (since it's not creating a new resource)\n   - Handles the idempotent case: if already CONFIRMED, returns it unchanged (no error)\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**: Add four new tests:\n   - `confirms a created shipment moves to confirmed` - happy path\n   - `confirming a confirmed shipment succeeds idempotently` - idempotent retry\n   - `confirming a cancelled shipment returns 409` - conflict case\n   - `confirming a non-existent shipment returns 404` - not found case\n\n**Alternative rejected:**\nI considered creating a separate ShipmentService layer to handle the state transition logic, but since the existing controller directly uses the repository with minimal logic (create just wraps the entity), adding the confirm logic directly to the controller is consistent with the baseline architecture. A service would be over-engineering for this simple operation and add an unnecessary file that the constraints discourage.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n- Happy path (CREATED→CONFIRMED): `POST /shipments/{id}/confirm` → Controller retrieves shipment from repo → Updates status → Saves → Returns 200 with updated entity\n- Idempotent path (already CONFIRMED): Same flow, status stays CONFIRMED, returns 200 with entity unchanged\n- Error path (CANCELLED): `POST /shipments/{id}/confirm` → Controller retrieves from repo → Throws ConflictException → GlobalExceptionHandler converts to 409 response with error envelope\n- Error path (not found): Throws ResourceNotFoundException → GlobalExceptionHandler converts to 404 response with error envelope\n\n**Test strategy:**\n- Test 1: Create a shipment in CREATED, confirm it, verify status becomes CONFIRMED, verify response has the shipment\n- Test 2: Confirm a shipment twice, verify both calls return 200 and the status remains CONFIRMED\n- Test 3: Create a shipment, manually set status to CANCELLED via repository, confirm it, verify 409 with correct error code\n- Test 4: Confirm a non-existent shipment ID, verify 404 with correct error code\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1202,"cache_read_input_tokens":18052,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1202},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"488e0151-fd10-47f0-b574-3bc4c0debd07","uuid":"ad35edf2-99a1-4fb1-a5f4-53f3e6fe1fb5","timestamp":"2026-09-09T15:57:13.850Z","request_id":"req_011Cet94bmteyrNTsWWuQQCZ"}
